# UI interaction rules

Apply these on every new or changed action surface.

## Pointer cursor

Every clickable uses `cursor-pointer` (links, buttons, menu items, clickable cards). Disabled controls use `cursor-not-allowed`. Prefer the shared `Button` and global CSS — do not add `cursor-default` on interactive elements.

## Button loaders

If an action waits on the network, set `:loading` on `Button`. The button must replace its label with the spinner, then restore the original label when the request finishes. Do not keep the original text beside the spinner.

```vue
<Button type="submit" :loading="processing">Save</Button>
```

## Delete confirmation

Never use `window.confirm` or a plain dialog for deletes. Use `ConfirmDeleteDialog` (glass popup) with a clear title, consequence, Cancel, and a destructive confirm button that uses `:loading`.

## Action feedback

Every action button must show a success or error message after it runs (toast via `notifySuccess` / `notifyError`, or an Inertia flash toast). Field errors can stay inline, but the user still gets a toast. Do not swallow failures.

```ts
notifySuccess('Profile updated.');
notifyError(firstValidationError(errors) ?? 'Something went wrong. Please try again.');
```
